# API module architecture

Follow `docs/architecture/api-modules.md` for all API work.

## Structure

- Wire dependencies in `AppContainer` (`apps/api/src/container/app-container.ts`).
- Routers are thin; HTTP handlers live in `controllers/` classes extending `BaseController` or `OrganizationScopedController`.
- Business logic in `services/` **classes** with constructor injection.
- Use `repositories/` when Prisma logic is shared or complex (see `modules/storage/`).
- Do not add business logic to `routes/v1.ts` or middleware beyond cross-cutting concerns.

## Naming

- Files: `*.router.ts`, `*.controller.ts`, `*.service.ts`, `*.repository.ts`
- Classes: `AuthController`, `AuthService`, `SessionManager`, `CookieManager`
- Prefer `new ClassName(deps)` registered on `AppContainer` over new standalone `createX()` factories.

## Types and validation

- Request/params/query: Zod in `@vaultstack/validation` + `validateBody` / `validateParams` / `validateQuery`.
- Public responses: `@vaultstack/types` (`Public*`).
- Request metadata: `RequestMeta` from `@vaultstack/types`.
- No `any`; no duplicate validation in controllers.

## Security (mandatory)

- Crypto/tokens/passwords only via `@vaultstack/auth` classes or `SessionManager` / `AuthenticationService` / `StorageTokenManager`.
- Never log secrets, tokens, or password material.
- Never store file binaries or raw tokens in PostgreSQL.
- Check permissions server-side before destructive operations.
- Cookie auth: HTTP-only session cookie + CSRF header on mutations.

## Before finishing

- [ ] New services registered on `AppContainer`
- [ ] Tests for behavior changes
- [ ] API docs/OpenAPI sync if routes or shapes changed (see `api-docs-sync.mdc`)
